1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
The turning point was realizing that speed is not the same thing as progress.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:20,000
We were shipping more features every week, but users were taking longer to reach a useful result.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:30,000
So we replaced the feature target with one question: can a new person succeed in ten minutes?

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:40,000
That constraint felt slower at first because it forced us to remove work we had already completed.

5
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Within a month, support requests fell and the team spent less time explaining the product.

6
00:00:50,000 --> 00:01:00,000
The lesson is simple: progress is the distance removed between a person and a meaningful outcome.
